      "id": "xu-zhimo-poems-s0030-p00030",
      "source_en": "I looked up at the ancient, weathered mountains; they did not utter a single word. The sunlight drew out my insignificance, while the blades of grass lay beneath my feet. I stopped alone by the roadside, listening to the wind-borne pines in the empty valley. In the blue sky, white clouds once nestled there, and in the blink of an eye they were gone.",
